Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: hull shader vPrim, indexed patch constants and control points

Three hull-shader constructs that fxc emits for the DirectX SDK (June 2010)
SubD11 sample were rejected by the TGSI translation. Each rejection made
CreateHullShader call pfnSetErrorCb(E_INVALIDARG), which the D3D11 runtime
turns into device removal, so the sample's device-created callback failed
with DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED ("An error occurred in the device create
callback function", then DXUT's "non-zero reference count" dialog).

1. SV_PrimitiveID. "dcl_input vPrim" has operand type
   D3D10_SB_OPERAND_TYPE_INPUT_PRIMITIVEID and no index. dcl_tess_input sent
   it to the control-point path, which needs a two-dimensional operand
   ("invalid-control-point-input-declaration"). Declare TGSI_SEMANTIC_PRIMID
   as a system value once (a hull shader declares vPrim again in every phase
   that reads it), as dcl_gs_input does for geometry shaders.

2. dcl_indexrange over ordinary patch constants. A fork phase with an
   instance count writes o[r0.x + 6].x with "dcl_indexrange o6.x 8"; the
   translation accepted output ranges over tessellation factors only.
   Ordinary patch constants are separate TGSI PATCH outputs, so the indexed
   store goes through the same select-and-store sequence as tessellation
   factors (emit_tcs_indexed_output_stores), with the store's own component
   mask. A range may cover registers the phase does not declare itself
   (D3DCompiler_43 emits "dcl_indexrange o14.x 6" with only o14 and o17-o19
   declared in that phase); those are declared on first use. A range may not
   mix tessellation factors and ordinary patch constants.

3. dcl_indexrange over input control points, and reads of
   vicp[r0.y + 0][r0.x + 1]. dcl_input_index_range accepted one-dimensional
   input ranges only. Accept vicp[n][r] and v[n][r] ranges (the first
   register is the second index). For a relative register index the reader
   selects among the inputs of the range; each candidate is now read at the
   vertex index (translate_indexed_vertex_input). Before, the vertex
   dimension was applied to the selected temporary, which has none; this
   also affected geometry shaders reading v[n][r + i].

probes/d3d11-tess/tess_probe.exe checks every construct against values
computed on the CPU (and against WARP).

Evidence: docs/d3d11-apps.md, docs/evidence/d3d11-apps/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d fix-d3d11-apps worker.
